A||N||5||Anthony||Putting a 5 speed getrang into 86 with a 4speed||||5
Z||000000||Anthony||11-11-1999||11:33 PM||||Can I replace my 4 speed with a 5 speed getrang and if so what wil I have to change to make it work,Also I have heard GM makes themm for other front wheel drive cars,would they work?.thanks again||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||11-11-1999||11:46 PM||||It'll work. Also, late 80's Getrags from other GM cars will work, with some mods.<BR>See Rodney Dickman's site for details and parts. <BR>    <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Anthony||11-11-1999||11:55 PM||||Is this just a drop in swap or is there any other mods that have to be made||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||11-12-1999||07:40 AM||||I think you'll have to replace the shifter (not sure about this). Maybe the slave cylinder. Most of the mods are to the trans itself. Involve brackets and levers and such. Think the axles are different. Rodney's site has a wealth of info.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Thomas||11-12-1999||08:05 AM||||I´ve done this swap. Its works.<BR>Swap too:<BR>Schift Knop<BR>Schift cabel (both)<BR>Clutch Pedal(87 Pedal ist better )not necessary<BR>ECM ROM and call pack<BR>Slave cylinder (include heat shield and holder)<BR>Clutch Disk ( I mean the metalplate at the Engine. I´ve forgot the name)<P>But a better idea is to swap the comlete Engine include the cradle too. It is easier.<P>The reverse switch in an 5 Gear is direkt at the Gearbox.<BR>In a 4 Gear at the shift knob.<BR>I found all cable for both version in my car.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Formula||11-12-1999||12:55 PM||||The 4 spd transmission accelerates faster.......not as good gas mpg||||reg||1
